            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Carex arenaria, or sand sedge, is a species of perennial sedge of the genus Carex which is commonly found growing in dunes and other sandy habitats, as the species epithet suggests (Latin {{lang|la|[[:wikt:arenarius|arenarius]]}}, \"sandy\"). It grows by long stolons under the soil surface."
